From b21a94b90f7c3c215139c0b3b715d8da24f7f80d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khushal Verma <codzentechnology@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:35:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade zod 3 -> 4 and drop unused @hookform/resolvers

Fixes the high-severity zod advisory (GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5, memory exhaustion
validating oversized collections). No schema here uses arrays, so the app was
not exposed, but the fix is free: all validation code is unchanged and passes
type-check, tests, lint and build. `npm audit --omit=dev` now reports 0.

@hookform/resolvers was copied over from the HRMS package.json and is not
imported anywhere.

The remaining moderate findings are the tailwindcss -> postcss-selector-parser
build-time chain, which has no upstream fix and never sees user input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K84HrvUpcXKwbefK6HRaKf
